BT /F2 7.8 Tf 42.0 763.0 Td (1. What is an enum class and Why is it Superior to Old C Enums?) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 36.0 758.0 Td (Traditional C-style enums \('enum Color { RED, GREEN };'\) possess two severe architectural flaws: they export their enumeration names) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 36.0 747.5 Td (directly into the surrounding scope \(causing name clashes\), and they implicitly convert to integers without type checking. C++11 introduced) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 36.0 737.0 Td (scoped enumerations \('enum class'\), which enforce strict type safety and require explicit scope resolution.) Tj ET
